===== run 1 diagnosis (from: nix log /nix/store/ppdcxmdsrrq4mn8hnjp4v852h13z7flh-vm-test-run-iso-autostart-vm.drv) =====
The initrd activation aborts at the bootstrapPasswordHash validator (missing
/var/lib/nixos-bootstrap/mei-password.hash); /etc never lands, so systemd's
switch-root refuses and the test framework's panic-on-fail kills the VM:
  [    4.04] initrd-nixos-activation-start[209]: bootstrap password hash validation failed: missing /var/lib/nixos-bootstrap/mei-password.hash
  [    4.07] @ystemctl[217]: Failed to switch root: Specified switch root path '/sysroot' does not seem to be an OS tree. os-release file is missing.
  [    4.36] sysrq: Trigger a crash
  [    4.36] Kernel panic - not syncing: sysrq triggered crash
  => RuntimeError: Shell disconnected (test driver).
Fix (test-only, documented in tests/iso-autostart-vm.nix): seed the installed
machine's verifier file in the initrd before activation; memory 2048 / cores 2.
Note: flake.isoConfig.antagony.config has boot.initrd.{enable,systemd.enable}=true,
so the same fresh-boot activation abort applies to the real ISO config; recorded
as a config-level finding (out of lane scope, not fixed here).
